# Conversion — Hard Requirement

Beautiful with no clear next step is a fail.

## Choose the action from the business

Decide the single primary action from what this business actually sells, then design the whole page around it.

| Business | Primary action |
| --- | --- |
| Plumber, locksmith, electrician, tow | Call now |
| Restaurant, bistro | Book a table |
| Salon, barber, small trade | WhatsApp |
| Walk-in shop, showroom | Get directions |
| Contractor, installer | Request a quote |
| Takeaway | Order |

This table is a prompt, not a lookup. Read the business and pick what actually converts for it.

## Rules

- The primary CTA must be reachable within one thumb movement at any scroll position on mobile. A persistent bar, dock, or floating action is usually right — decide the pattern from the design, not from habit.
- Every CTA fires a real mechanism: `tel:`, `https://wa.me/<number>`, a maps deep link, a mailto, or a real booking URL. No dead buttons, no `href="#"`, no fake forms.
- Label the outcome. "Call the shop", "WhatsApp us", "Book a table" — never "Learn more", "Get started", or "Click here".
- Secondary actions support the primary one and never compete with it visually.
- Contact details, address, and opening hours are findable without scrolling the whole page, and match the JSON-LD exactly.
- Unknown detail → clearly-labelled placeholder plus a line in the outreach issue asking the owner to confirm. Never invent a phone number or address.
